# 200 · A plateau stop: a run ends after a time without a new champion, when the owner sets it

**Status:** `PROPOSED` · **Version:** [v0.1.4](../roadmap.md#v014)

## What

From [issue 50](https://github.com/iammrduncan/thermite/issues/50), the field report's fourth request. Nothing ends a run that has stopped improving: in the report, one run spent about 5 hours of GPU time after its last gain. A contract or run setting, such as `stop_after_minutes_without_champion`, closes or pauses the run (the owner chooses which) once that long has passed without a new champion. Off unless set.

## Why

A stuck run holds a GPU that the next target could use.

## Constraints

- **No default caps.** Off unless the owner sets it.

## Done when

- [ ] The setting, with tests: a run with it set stops after the time without a champion; one without it never stops for this.
- [ ] Pages: the contract's reference, Budget and stop time, and the changelog.

## Decisions

- None yet.

## Progress

- 2026-11-03: Goal written for v0.1.3's plan, from the open issues of its milestone.

